      "created_at": "2014-08-26T09:58:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"j1hopki1\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/58f4c7/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> j1hopki1:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Cosmonaut Zero wrote:</b><br><blockquote>If you know something has gender but don't know what that &nbsp;gender is, \"they\" is an appropriate usage.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nIf you know Omnitron-X does not have a gender, is \"they\" still appropriate?\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes.&nbsp; The singular \"they\" is all-inclusive.&nbsp; (The plural is \"all them\".)</p>",
